---
import { Braces, Camera, CircleQuestionMark, ShieldCheck, SlidersHorizontal } from "@lucide/astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Sift approaches reliability"
  description="Learn how Sift constrains AI analysis with structured outputs, server and client validation, deterministic safety floors, explicit Unclear results, and failure-mode evaluation."
  path="/reliability"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Reliability"
    title="Confidence should come from the method, not a magic number."
    description="Sift uses AI to review imperfect menu information, then surrounds that output with structure, validation, conservative rules, and an explicit way to say ‘not enough information.’"
    compact
  />

  <section class="method-intro" aria-labelledby="method-intro-title">
    <div class="shell method-intro__inner">
      <h2 id="method-intro-title">AI is one part of a constrained path.</h2>
      <p>
        Menu analysis is not a single prompt followed by a verdict. The source image, the requested structure, the
        checks around the response, and the way uncertainty is presented all affect whether a result is useful.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <div class="shell method__layout">
      <div class="method__heading">
        <h2 id="method-title">The analysis path</h2>
        <p>Each stage is designed to preserve context and prevent weak information from looking more certain than it is.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="method__steps">
        <li>
          <span class="method__number">01</span>
          <Camera size={23} stroke-width={1.7} aria-hidden="true" />
          <div>
            <h3>Inputs stay specific.</h3>
            <p>
              Sift analyzes the menu image selected by the user in the context of that user's allergy profile. Image
              readability is part of the result, because a blurred or incomplete source changes what can be inferred.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="method__number">02</span>
          <Braces size={23} stroke-width={1.7} aria-hidden="true" />
          <div>
            <h3>The model must return a defined structure.</h3>
            <p>
              The response is expected to separate an overall status from per-dish reasoning, possible allergens,
              hidden-risk patterns, cross-contact concerns, staff questions, readability, and source references.
              That makes the output checkable instead of leaving it as free-form prose.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="method__number">03</span>
          <ShieldCheck size={23} stroke-width={1.7} aria-hidden="true" />
          <div>
            <h3>The server validates before the app accepts it.</h3>
            <p>
              Server-side checks verify required fields, allowed status values, and basic consistency. Malformed,
              missing, or contradictory data is not treated as a complete analysis.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="method__number">04</span>
          <SlidersHorizontal size={23} stroke-width={1.7} aria-hidden="true" />
          <div>
            <h3>The client validates again and applies deterministic floors.</h3>
            <p>
              The app checks the result before rendering it. Conditions such as insufficient image detail, missing
              required evidence, contradictory fields, or a validation failure can only move the experience toward
              more caution; they cannot be promoted into a reassuring status.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="method__number">05</span>
          <CircleQuestionMark size={23} stroke-width={1.7} aria-hidden="true" />
          <div>
            <h3>Unclear is a first-class outcome.</h3>
            <p>
              If Sift cannot support a useful interpretation, it says <strong>Unclear</strong> and directs the user to
              retake the photo or ask staff. The system is not designed to fill an information gap with false
              confidence.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <div class="shell evidence__layout">
      <div class="evidence__copy">
        <h2 id="evidence-title">The app shows what sits underneath the status.</h2>
        <p>
          A risk label is a starting point. Sift keeps the visible checks, limitations, and dish-level reasoning close
          enough for the diner to inspect before deciding what to ask.
        </p>

        <ul class="margin-notes">
          <li>
            <span>Input quality</span>
            The result reports whether the menu image was readable enough to interpret.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Scope</span>
            The summary names what Sift checked and calls out when external restaurant sources were not returned.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Reasoning</span>
            Dish details separate possible allergens, hidden-risk ingredients, cross-contact concerns, and questions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Boundary</span>
            The interface repeats that Sift cannot guarantee a dish is safe.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <figure class="evidence__screens">
        <img
          class="evidence__summary"
          src="/app/results-top.png"
          alt="Sift scan summary showing image readability, what the app checked, and the no-guarantee safety notice"
          width="390"
          height="844"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <img
          class="evidence__detail"
          src="/app/dish-detail-reasoning.png"
          alt="Sift dish detail showing possible allergens, hidden-risk ingredients, cross-contact concerns, and staff questions"
          width="390"
          height="844"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>Current Sift screens. The summary and its supporting detail are both available to the user.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="evaluation" aria-labelledby="evaluation-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="evaluation__heading">
        <h2 id="evaluation-title">Evaluate the ways the system can fail.</h2>
        <p>
          A useful evaluation separates failure modes instead of averaging them into one flattering score. These are
          the categories Sift's validation program is designed to examine.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="evaluation__table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Reliability evaluation table">
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Sift evaluation categories and the failures each category is intended to expose</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Failure mode</th>
              <th scope="col">What is examined</th>
              <th scope="col">What must not be hidden</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Image and text capture</th>
              <td>Blur, crop, glare, small type, layout, and language conditions.</td>
              <td>Unreadable or missing menu information.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Listed-allergen recall</th>
              <td>Whether visible allergen terms relevant to the user's profile are surfaced.</td>
              <td>Missed concerns, especially when the app sounds reassuring.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Hidden-risk reasoning</th>
              <td>Whether common ingredient or preparation patterns are raised with appropriate uncertainty.</td>
              <td>Speculation presented as fact, or common patterns omitted without explanation.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Cross-contact guidance</th>
              <td>Whether the result prompts relevant staff questions without claiming to know kitchen practice.</td>
              <td>Implied knowledge of fryers, surfaces, utensils, suppliers, or preparation areas.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Calibration and fallback</th>
              <td>Whether status, reasoning, and image quality agree—and whether weak evidence becomes Unclear.</td>
              <td>Contradictions, malformed output, or false confidence.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="metric" aria-labelledby="metric-title">
    <div class="shell metric__layout">
      <h2 id="metric-title">Why there is no single “accuracy” percentage</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          One number can collapse very different tasks: reading a menu, matching an allergy term, reasoning about a
          common preparation pattern, choosing an appropriately cautious status, and recognizing when the evidence is
          insufficient. Those errors do not carry the same consequence, and performance can change with allergen,
          language, menu format, and image quality.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sift will only publish measured reliability claims with the test scope, method, sample, and limitations beside
          them. A percentage without that context would be easier to market and harder to trust.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="status-note" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <div class="shell status-note__inner">
      <ShieldCheck size={34} stroke-width={1.6} aria-hidden="true" />
      <div>
        <h2 id="status-title">Current validation status</h2>
        <p>
          Sift's full live validation gate is not yet complete. The structured checks and failure-mode evaluation plan
          described here are safeguards and methodology—not proof of end-to-end production performance. Until that
          gate is complete, Sift does not publish an accuracy percentage or describe the system as production-validated.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/safety">Read the safety boundary <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .method-intro {
    padding-block: clamp(66px, 9vw, 108px);
  }

  .method-intro__inner {
    align-items: end;
    display: grid;
    gap: 28px clamp(44px, 9vw, 132px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.08fr) minmax(300px, 0.72fr);
  }

  .method-intro h2,
  .method-intro p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .method-intro p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .method {
    background: var(--teal-900);
    color: var(--white);
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 124px);
  }

  .method__layout {
    display: grid;
    gap: 46px clamp(56px, 10vw, 150px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 1.45fr);
  }

  .method__heading {
    align-self: start;
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-height) + 42px);
  }

  .method__heading h2 {
    color: var(--white);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .method__heading p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    max-width: 34ch;
  }

  .method__steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .method__steps li {
    align-items: start;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24);
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px 22px;
    grid-template-columns: 42px 30px minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: 30px 34px;
  }

  .method__steps li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24);
  }

  .method__number {
    color: var(--tangerine);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-top: 5px;
  }

  .method__steps svg {
    color: var(--teal-100);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .method__steps h3 {
    color: var(--white);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2vw, 1.72rem);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .method__steps p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .method__steps strong {
    color: var(--white);
  }

  .evidence {
    padding-block: clamp(78px, 11vw, 142px);
  }

  .evidence__layout {
    align-items: center;
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(54px, 9vw, 132px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.82fr) minmax(440px, 1.18fr);
  }

  .evidence__copy h2 {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .evidence__copy > p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: 36px;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .margin-notes {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .margin-notes li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: #34433f;
    padding-block: 18px;
  }

  .margin-notes li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .margin-notes span {
    color: var(--teal-700);
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }

  .evidence__screens {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 700px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .evidence__screens img {
    background: var(--cream);
    border-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-phone);
    position: absolute;
  }

  .evidence__summary {
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: min(54%, 292px);
  }

  .evidence__detail {
    right: 0;
    top: 88px;
    width: min(50%, 268px);
  }

  .evidence__screens figcaption {
    bottom: 0;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin: 0;
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    width: min(58%, 310px);
  }

  .evaluation {
    background: var(--warm);
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 124px);
  }

  .evaluation__heading {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px clamp(40px, 8vw, 112px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(300px, 0.72fr);
    margin-bottom: clamp(44px, 7vw, 72px);
  }

  .evaluation__heading h2,
  .evaluation__heading p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .evaluation__heading p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .evaluation__table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .evaluation__table-wrap:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--teal-600);
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }

  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    min-width: 820px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  th,
  td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 20px 24px 22px 0;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  thead th {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    padding-block: 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  tbody th {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    width: 24%;
  }

  tbody td {
    color: #34433f;
    width: 38%;
  }

  .visually-hidden {
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: absolute;
    white-space: nowrap;
    width: 1px;
  }

  .metric {
    padding-block: clamp(78px, 11vw, 138px);
  }

  .metric__layout {
    display: grid;
    gap: 36px clamp(54px, 10vw, 148px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(360px, 1.2fr);
  }

  .metric h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.7rem);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .metric p {
    color: #34433f;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .metric p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .status-note {
    background: var(--teal-100);
    padding-block: clamp(54px, 7vw, 78px);
  }

  .status-note__inner {
    align-items: start;
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px clamp(28px, 5vw, 68px);
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(190px, auto);
  }

  .status-note svg {
    color: var(--teal-700);
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .status-note h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .status-note p {
    color: #29433f;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .status-note a {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--teal-600);
    color: var(--teal-800);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    justify-self: end;
    padding-bottom: 7px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .method-intro__inner,
    .method__layout,
    .evidence__layout,
    .evaluation__heading,
    .metric__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .method__heading {
      position: static;
    }

    .method__heading p {
      max-width: 58ch;
    }

    .evidence__screens {
      margin-inline: auto;
      max-width: 600px;
      min-height: 680px;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .status-note__inner {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .status-note a {
      grid-column: 2;
      justify-self: start;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .method__steps li {
      gap: 12px 14px;
      grid-template-columns: 34px 26px minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .method__steps p {
      font-size: 0.96rem;
    }

    .evidence__screens {
      min-height: 540px;
    }

    .evidence__screens img {
      border-radius: 18px;
    }

    .evidence__summary {
      width: 218px;
    }

    .evidence__detail {
      top: 72px;
      width: 205px;
    }

    .evidence__screens figcaption {
      width: 230px;
    }

    .status-note__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .status-note a {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 390px) {
    .evidence__screens {
      min-height: 500px;
    }

    .evidence__summary,
    .evidence__detail {
      width: 190px;
    }
  }
</style>
